      "podcast_title": "From Bee-Bots to Backend Breaches",
      "podcast_desc": "This podcast episode features an interview with Ruben Spillebeen, a software developer who works on backend systems for a Belgian union. The discussion highlights his non-traditional career path, starting with visual tools like Scratch and moving into professional development with .NET and Angular. Ruben explains his daily responsibilities, which involve managing large-scale document processing and ensuring system security through automated checks and internal reviews. The conversation also explores the practical use of AI tools like GitHub Copilot and the importance of clean code standards in a team of fifty developers. Finally, Ruben offers advice to students, emphasizing that while security is paramount, developers often rely on senior peer reviews and specialized frameworks to catch vulnerabilities before release.",
